I left out `aap:caps/http-client` because this node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and the enrichment call would send digest text to an external host. The output would be unchanged, but the call would still reach outside the granted authority. The notifier-only version below is what the contract allows.

```wit
package gen:node;

use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

world node {
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for entry in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str("\n- ");
            message.push_str(&entry.title);
            message.push(' ');
            message.push_str(&entry.link);
        }

        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

